Introduction:
This project aims to check whether a student is eligible for a scholarship based on their academic score and annual family income.
The system checks both details according to the given eligibility rules and provides the result. It helps the university identify eligible 
students easily and reduces the time required for manually checking scholarship applications.

Prompt:
Check the student's academic score and annual family income using the given scholarship eligibility criteria.
A student is eligible only if their academic score is at least 85% and their annual family income is ₹3,00,000 or less.
Both conditions must be satisfied to qualify for the scholarship. If any required information is missing, return INSUFFICIENT_DATA. Otherwise,
return ELIGIBLE or NOT_ELIGIBLE based on the criteria. Provide only the correct result without any explanation or additional text.

